    "longDescription": "I'm having a problem displaying maps from OpenStreetMap on the Leaflet API server. The essential requirements I got from their website for displaying a street map are: Disabling Tracking Prevention Specifying a browser User Agent Displaying the attribution Resend the referrer property I'm having a problem with making request for loading street map image tiles from OpenStreetMap API into the HTML control. I'm using the Microsoft control WebView2 to display the HTML page. I may be missing other policy requirements are not properly implementing the ones I do have. I assume the resource event is fired automatically. Microsoft Copilot suggest the following code snippet for my implementation: private async Task InitializeWebView2Async() { var options = new CoreWebView2EnvironmentOptions { EnableTrackingPrevention = false }; var environment = await CoreWebView2Environment.CreateAsync(options: options); await MapView.EnsureCoreWebView2Async(environment); MapView.CoreWebView2.WebResourceRequested += CoreWebView2_WebResourceRequested; } private void CoreWebView2_WebResourceRequested(object sender, CoreWebView2WebResourceRequestedEventArgs e) { try { // Add or update headers for every outbound request. e.Request.Headers.SetHeader(\"User Agent\", \"Mozilla/5\"); //e.Request.Headers.SetHeader(\"User Agent\", \"Edge\"); var referrer = MapView.Source?.AbsoluteUri; if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(referrer)) { e.Request.Headers.SetHeader(\"Referer\", referrer); } // I guess at the syntax for the browser agent parameters } catch (Exception ex) { Console.WriteLine($\"Error setting headers: {ex.Message}\"); } } When I select the street view, I get the following Map display: However, when I select the terrain view, I get the following display: I can get away with using the Terrain maps, but I would also like to have the option for street maps if possible. Thanks I got the following code snippet from: https://tutorials.dodatech.com/frontend/libraries/leafletjs/leafletjs-tile-layers/ <!DOCTYPE html> <html> <head> <title>Tile Layers Demo</title> <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9/dist/leaflet.css\" /> <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9/dist/leaflet.js\"></script> </head> <body style=\"font-family:sans-serif;padding:20px;\"> <h2>Tile Layer Switching</h2> <div id=\"map\" style=\"height:400px;border-radius:8px;\"></div> <script> var map = L.map('map').setView([40.7128, -74.0060], 12); var street = L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', { attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap' }); var dark = L.tileLayer('https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/dark_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', { attribution: '&copy; CARTO' }); var terrain = L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.opentopomap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', { attribution: '&copy; OpenTopoMap' }); L.control.layers({ 'Street': street, 'Dark': dark, 'Terrain': terrain }).addTo(map); street.addTo(map); </script> </body> </html> If you wish to use my demo code: <!-- Source - https://stackoverflow.com/a/80016565 Posted by Greg Burghardt, modified by community. See post 'Timeline' for change history Retrieved 2026-11-15, License - CC BY-SA 4.0 --> <!DOCTYPE html> <html lang=\"en\"> <head> <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" /> <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" /> <title>OSRM + OpenStreetMap Route (No Google Key)</title> <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css\" crossorigin=\"\" /> <style> html, body, #map { height: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0; } .notice { position: absolute; top: 10px; left: 10px; z-index: 1000; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, * 0.95); padding: 10px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; border-radius: 4px; box-shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2); max-width: 430px; line-height: 1.35; } .notice a { color: #0b57d0; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; } </style> </head> <body> <div class=\"notice\" id=\"status\">Loading route from OSRM...</div> <div id=\"map\"></div> <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js\" crossorigin></script> <script> // Marker points (latitude, longitude) const start = { lat: 44.9778, lng: -93.2650 }; const end = { lat: 44.9537, lng: -93.0900 }; const map = L.map(\"map\").setView([start.lat, start.lng], 12); /************************************************************ * The Fix: use L.TileLayer instead of TileLayer *********************************************************** new L.TileLayer(\"https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png\", { attribution: \"&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors\", maxZoom: 18 }).addTo(map); ***********************************************************/ /******************************************************************** * The Updated Fix: Only Terrain (opentopomap) custom layer works in this demo. * https://tutorials.dodatech.com/frontend/libraries/leafletjs/leafletjs-tile-layers/ *******************************************************************/ var street = L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', { attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap' }); var dark = L.tileLayer('https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/dark_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', { attribution: '&copy; CARTO' }); var terrain = L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.opentopomap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', { attribution: '&copy; OpenTopoMap' }); L.control.layers({ 'Street': street, 'Dark': dark, 'Terrain': terrain }).addTo(map); terrain.addTo(map); /******************************************************************/ L.marker([start.lat, start.lng]).addTo(map).bindPopup(\"Start\"); L.marker([end.lat, end.lng]).addTo(map).bindPopup(\"End\"); function formatMeters(meters) { if (meters < 1000) { return `${Math.round(meters)} m`; } return `${(meters / 1000).toFixed(1)} km`; } function formatSeconds(seconds) { const totalMinutes = Math.round(seconds / 60); const hours = Math.floor(totalMinutes / 60); const minutes = totalMinutes % 60; if (hours === 0) { return `${minutes} min`; } return `${hours}h ${minutes}m`; } function buildGoogleMapsDirectionsLink(startPoint, endPoint) { const origin = `${startPoint.lat},${startPoint.lng}`; const destination = `${endPoint.lat},${endPoint.lng}`; return `https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=${encodeURIComponent(origin)}&destination=${encodeURIComponent(destination)}&travelmode=driving`; } async function drawRoute() { const status = document.getElementById(\"status\"); const osrmUrl = `https://router.project-osrm.org/route/v1/driving/${start.lng},${start.lat};${end.lng},${end.lat}?overview=full&geometries=geojson`; try { const response = await fetch(osrmUrl); if (!response.ok) { throw new Error(`OSRM HTTP ${response.status}`); } const data = await response.json(); if (!data.routes || data.routes.length === 0) { throw new Error(\"OSRM returned no routes.\"); } const route = data.routes[0]; const latLngs = route.geometry.coordinates.map(c => [c[1], c[0]]); const line = L.polyline(latLngs, { color: \"#1A73E8\", weight: 5, opacity: 0.95 }).addTo(map); map.fitBounds(line.getBounds(), { padding: [20, 20] }); const googleLink = buildGoogleMapsDirectionsLink(start, end); status.innerHTML = `${formatMeters(route.distance)} • ${formatSeconds(route.duration)}<br/>` + `Route drawn with OSRM + OSM (no Google key). ` + `<a href=\"${googleLink}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open same markers in Google Maps</a>`; } catch (error) { console.error(error); status.textContent = `Unable to draw route: ${error.message}`; } } drawRoute(); </script> </body> </html>",
